  "notes": "Thermal-runaway propagation experiments on multi-cell modules; measurements are MATLAB table objects (also given as txt): cell voltages, cell temperatures, venting temperatures and surface temperatures. The landing page (mediaTUM) is behind a bot check, so no description could be read. Both delivered electrode-system folders explicitly identify graphite (GraphiteLFP and GraphiteNMC-811). The two extracted entities are modules, not two individual cells; the author surface-temperature READMEs reference cells 1 through 5 within each module. Temperature includes cell, venting and module-surface channels; cached combined extrema do not isolate cell sensors."
=======
  "notes": "Thermal-runaway propagation experiments on multi-cell modules; measurements are MATLAB table objects (also given as txt): cell voltages, cell temperatures, venting temperatures and surface temperatures. Both delivered electrode-system folders explicitly identify graphite (GraphiteLFP and GraphiteNMC-811). The two extracted entities are modules, not two individual cells; the author surface-temperature READMEs reference cells 1 through 5 within each module. Temperature includes cell, venting and module-surface channels; cached combined extrema do not isolate cell sensors. Charging profile: null: abuse (thermal runaway) tests; no charge protocol. The article (Schoberl et al., eTransportation 19 (2024) 100305; full text read) describes the data: five CATL prismatic hardcase cells (two jelly rolls each) per module, Graphite | NMC-811 from a MINI Cooper SE (96.3 Ah, 3.65 V, 173 x 42 x 85 mm, 1420 g) and Graphite | LFP from a Tesla Model 3 SR+ (163.3 Ah, 3.2 V, 280 x 63 x 82 mm, 3100 g), the capacities determined by a CC C/3 discharge (so measured, not rated; the NMC data come from the data sheet and own measurements, the LFP data from teardown studies); cells charged to 100% SOC at C/10 CCCV, braced at 30% SOC with 65 kPa preload (1000 N and 1500 N), overheating trigger on the first cell, type K thermocouples between the cells and at the safety vents, a FLIR A70 thermal camera (surface temperatures qualitative only) and cell voltages through an imc CANSASflex module. The cell model names are not given, and the per-cell dimensions are not recorded because the schema holds one set of dimensions per dataset. The entities in the data are the two modules; the DOI of the data is 10.14459/2023mp1717758 (mediaTUM)."
